  playerLines:
  - <i>Aleph</i> huh...
  - <i>A way to denote one of the many possible infinities, borring a character from
    the Hebrew alphabet<i>
  - <i>Introduced by George Cantor to discretize the infinite cardinalities of sets<i>
  - ...
  - neat.
  - huh.
  - Well yeah, I don't really get big numbers like that
